# TF_GLM_LOOP_GUARD=1 ends a think block that has collapsed into repeating itself (issues #89 and #94; upstream
# ashhart/TensorFold#210 proposed a guard for the Zig engine only, closed unmerged). Per request, on the tokens the target committed, while
# the think block is open: an exact cycle of at most 16 tokens that held for 256 tokens ("maybe maybe maybe ..."), or
# one token taking half of the last 256 (a block that is mostly "the"). The next round's tokens are then replaced by the
# thinking budget's close (newline, </think>, blank line) through the same gate, so the model answers from there. Off by
# default (TF_GLM_LOOP_GUARD=0): nothing is built and no request changes. Requests that do not think never arm it.
# The reply's usage stats carry loop_guard: N when it fired. It does not catch paraphrase loops, which only
# --thinking-budget bounds. Earlier turns' looped reasoning is still resent by agents: TF_GLM_CLEAR_THINKING=1 drops it.

